  25:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****                         ##### How to use this driver #####
  26:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****   ==============================================================================
  27:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****     [..]
  28:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****       The SPI HAL driver can be used as follows:
  29:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  30:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) Declare a SPI_HandleTypeDef handle structure, for example:
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccMpXq91.s 			page 2


  31:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           SPI_HandleTypeDef  hspi;
  32:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  33:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#)Initialize the SPI low level resources by implementing the HAL_SPI_MspInit() API:
  34:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) Enable the SPIx interface clock
  35:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) SPI pins configuration
  36:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Enable the clock for the SPI GPIOs
  37:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Configure these SPI pins as alternate function push-pull
  38:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) NVIC configuration if you need to use interrupt process
  39:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Configure the SPIx interrupt priority
  40:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Enable the NVIC SPI IRQ handle
  41:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) DMA Configuration if you need to use DMA process
  42:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Declare a DMA_HandleTypeDef handle structure for the transmit or receive Stream
  43:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Enable the DMAx clock
  44:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Configure the DMA handle parameters
  45:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Configure the DMA Tx or Rx Stream/Channel
  46:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Associate the initialized hdma_tx(or _rx)  handle to the hspi DMA Tx or Rx hand
  47:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Configure the priority and enable the NVIC for the transfer complete interrupt 
  48:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****                     or Rx Stream/Channel
  49:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  50:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) Program the Mode, BidirectionalMode , Data size, Baudrate Prescaler, NSS
  51:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           management, Clock polarity and phase, FirstBit and CRC configuration in the hspi Init str
  52:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  53:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) Initialize the SPI registers by calling the HAL_SPI_Init() API:
  54:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           (++) This API configures also the low level Hardware GPIO, CLOCK, CORTEX...etc)
  55:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****               by calling the customized HAL_SPI_MspInit() API.
  56:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****      [..]
  57:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        Circular mode restriction:
  58:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) The DMA circular mode cannot be used when the SPI is configured in these modes:
  59:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) Master 2Lines RxOnly
  60:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) Master 1Line Rx
  61:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) The CRC feature is not managed when the DMA circular mode is enabled
  62:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) When the SPI DMA Pause/Stop features are used, we must use the following APIs
  63:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           the HAL_SPI_DMAPause()/ HAL_SPI_DMAStop() only under the SPI callbacks
  64:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****      [..]
  65:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        Master Receive mode restriction:
  66:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) In Master unidirectional receive-only mode (MSTR =1, BIDIMODE=0, RXONLY=1) or
  67:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           bidirectional receive mode (MSTR=1, BIDIMODE=1, BIDIOE=0), to ensure that the SPI
  68:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           does not initiate a new transfer the following procedure has to be respected:
  69:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) HAL_SPI_DeInit()
  70:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) HAL_SPI_Init()
  71:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****      [..]
  72:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        Callback registration:
  73:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  74:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) The compilation flag USE_HAL_SPI_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1U
  75:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
  76:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           Use Functions HAL_SPI_RegisterCallback() to register an interrupt callback.
  77:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  78:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           Function HAL_SPI_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
  79:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxCpltCallback        : SPI Tx Completed callback
  80:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) RxCpltCallback        : SPI Rx Completed callback
  81:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxRxCpltCallback      : SPI TxRx Completed callback
  82:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxHalfCpltCallback    : SPI Tx Half Completed callback
  83:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) RxHalfCpltCallback    : SPI Rx Half Completed callback
  84:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxRxHalfCpltCallback  : SPI TxRx Half Completed callback
  85:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) ErrorCallback         : SPI Error callback
  86:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) AbortCpltCallback     : SPI Abort callback
  87:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) MspInitCallback       : SPI Msp Init callback
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccMpXq91.s 			page 3


  88:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) MspDeInitCallback     : SPI Msp DeInit callback
  89:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
  90:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           and a pointer to the user callback function.
  91:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  92:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  93:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) Use function HAL_SPI_UnRegisterCallback to reset a callback to the default
  94:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           weak function.
  95:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           HAL_SPI_UnRegisterCallback takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
  96:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           and the Callback ID.
  97:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****           This function allows to reset following callbacks:
  98:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxCpltCallback        : SPI Tx Completed callback
  99:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) RxCpltCallback        : SPI Rx Completed callback
 100:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxRxCpltCallback      : SPI TxRx Completed callback
 101:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxHalfCpltCallback    : SPI Tx Half Completed callback
 102:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) RxHalfCpltCallback    : SPI Rx Half Completed callback
 103:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxRxHalfCpltCallback  : SPI TxRx Half Completed callback
 104:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) ErrorCallback         : SPI Error callback
 105:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) AbortCpltCallback     : SPI Abort callback
 106:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) MspInitCallback       : SPI Msp Init callback
 107:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) MspDeInitCallback     : SPI Msp DeInit callback
 108:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 109:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        [..]
 110:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        By default, after the HAL_SPI_Init() and when the state is HAL_SPI_STATE_RESET
 111:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 112:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        examples HAL_SPI_MasterTxCpltCallback(), HAL_SPI_MasterRxCpltCallback().
 113:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are
 114:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        reset to the legacy weak functions in the HAL_SPI_Init()/ HAL_SPI_DeInit() only when
 115:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 116:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        If MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_SPI_Init()/ HAL_SPI_DeInit()
 117:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand) whatever the state
 118:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 119:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        [..]
 120:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_SPI_STATE_READY state only.
 121:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit functions that can be registered/unregistered
 122:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        in HAL_SPI_STATE_READY or HAL_SPI_STATE_RESET state,
 123:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 124:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        Then, the user first registers the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 125:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        using HAL_SPI_RegisterCallback() before calling HAL_SPI_DeInit()
 126:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        or HAL_SPI_Init() function.
 127:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 128:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        [..]
 129:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        When the compilation define USE_HAL_PPP_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 130:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        not defined, the callback registering feature is not available
 131:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        and weak (surcharged) callbacks are used.
 132:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 133:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****      [..]
 134:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        Using the HAL it is not possible to reach all supported SPI frequency with the different SPI
 135:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****        the following table resume the max SPI frequency reached with data size 8bits/16bits,
 136:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c ****          according to frequency of the APBx Peripheral Clock (fPCLK) used by the SPI instance.
 137:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_spi.c **** 
